He wanted to get back to everyone quickly, so without thinking he reached in to grab the ball.
Just then, the concrete mixer, which shouldn't even have had the power on, suddenly started up.{p}

rows.08:9210:
After that, the ruined flower bed miraculously recovered, as lively as before, and began blooming vigorously again.
And her pneumonia, which had gotten so bad, strangely began to improve as well, as if keeping pace with the flowers.
She was finally able to leave the hospital, and she tended the flower bed with the other gardening members just as always.{p}

rows.08:95ec:
Maybe it's better for them this way.
After all, they get to soak up all the sunlight they want and bloom into beautiful flowers.
And maybe they drove away her illness so that Hayasaka would keep taking care of them forever.{p}

rows.08:a138:
At the school, the flowers were waiting.
"Everyone, I've come to say goodbye..."
In the rain, she went to each and every flower she had raised, tending it one last time and bidding it farewell.{p}

